00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:41.520
And what was the defining
characteristic of this

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.520
orthogonal projection vector p?
How did we find k star?

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:47.980
How did we know that this was
the right amount of v to take

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.600
and not some other amount?

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:54.350
What was the thinking there?

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:58.160
You drew a vector u minus kv,

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:02.860
and you know that that has to be
orthogonal to kv and so you know

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:05.320
their dot products can be zero
and then you can do algebra on

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:06.200
that.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:11.320
Good indeed the main idea is
that here p

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:15.240
is the orthogonal projection

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:26.060
of u onto v and the reason it is
the orthogonal projection

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:30.700
is because the error that is the
difference between u and that

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.960
