01:14:30.190 --> 01:14:32.850
Do we see the subtle difference
between these configurations?

01:14:32.850 --> 01:14:34.090
Either way,

01:14:34.090 --> 01:14:36.770
what we're dealing with is the
consequence of having three

01:14:36.770 --> 01:14:38.730
vectors in R2.

01:14:38.730 --> 01:14:39.630
No matter what,

01:14:39.630 --> 01:14:44.090
the most that any number of
vectors in R2 can span is all of

01:14:44.090 --> 01:14:44.890
R2.

01:14:44.890 --> 01:14:47.790
But the fact that we have some
extra redundant vectors

01:14:47.790 --> 01:14:50.970
actually will make things more
complicated, as we will see on

01:14:50.970 --> 01:14:52.510
Tuesday.
The fact that we have a third

01:14:52.510 --> 01:14:56.970
vector here now means that if we
try and go make a fourth vector

01:14:56.970 --> 01:15:00.590
using a linear combination of
